•Damage to our reputation, including as a result of failing to uphold our culture and the potential for the Internet and social media to magnify the effects of such reputational issues;

•Failure to meet our sustainability aspirations, goals and initiatives or to comply with increasingly complex climate-related and other sustainability regulations, heightened scrutiny, including a growing backlash against sustainability initiatives, and increased risks related to “greenwashing” and “greenhushing;”

